# Pairs with SeedCovered (review C1). A token removed without its close's
# re-claim leaves the abandoned attempt's seed in flight admissible, with no
# marker and no close heads to cover it.
MODULE: SeedCoveredAbortDropsToken
TARGET: SeedCovered
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: an abandoned attempt removes its switch token without a close
PERTURBS: Abort

--- FIND
    /\ aborted' = TRUE
    /\ phase' = "retry"
    /\ UNCHANGED <<next, author, rowsO, rpO, fO, narrowed, cst, cCounted, hint, tokOpen, prevOpen, prevHint,
--- REPLACE
    /\ aborted' = TRUE
    /\ phase' = "retry"
\* MUTATION: the token is dropped, unfenced.
    /\ tokOpen' = FALSE
    /\ UNCHANGED <<next, author, rowsO, rpO, fO, narrowed, cst, cCounted, hint, prevOpen, prevHint,
--- END
